# CODEOWNERS — routes review to whoever owns each area.
#
# TWO maintainers own the repository and review each other's changes:
#   Tim Coulter   @ynotbhatc
#   Juan Medina   @R0tt3nT0m4t0
# Because an author cannot approve their own PR, listing both on every rule
# means each change requires the OTHER maintainer's review — the two-approver
# model described in docs/CHANGE_GOVERNANCE.md §6. Add more team handles per
# area as the team grows.
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins, so every rule lists both owners.

# Default: everything
*                           @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0

# Product core — the handover surface an engineering team owns first
/ansible/roles/             @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
/ansible/tasks/             @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
/ansible/playbooks/         @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
/extensions/eda/            @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
/install/                   @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
/scripts/                   @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0

# Release + governance machinery — highest-scrutiny paths
/.github/                   @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
/VERSION                    @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
/RELEASING.md               @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
/CHANGELOG.md               @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
/docs/CHANGE_GOVERNANCE.md  @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0

# Policy library pointer (content gate lives in the submodule itself)
/policies                   @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0

# Demo content — migrates to the aac-demos repo at Phase 6; a separate
# demo-owning team can take these rows before then
/demos/                     @ynotbhatc @R0tt3nT0m4t0
